  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "Solve the inequality $5x\\cdot {3}^{x+1}+{3}^{x+1}\\ge -6\\cdot {3}^{x+1}.$\n\n$x$ \n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}",
  "worked_solution": "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x\\cdot {3}^{x+1}+{3}^{x+1} & \\ge -6\\cdot {3}^{x+1} \\\\ 5x\\cdot {3}^{x+1}+6\\cdot {3}^{x+1}+{3}^{x+1} & \\ge 0 \\\\ (5x+6+1){3}^{x+1} & \\ge 0 \\\\ (5x+7){3}^{x+1} & \\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by ${3}^{x+1}$ and solve the resulting inequality using familiar techniques:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(5x+7){3}^{x+1}}{{3}^{x+1}} & <\\frac{0}{{3}^{x+1}} \\\\ 5x+7 & \\ge 0 \\\\ 5x & \\ge 0-7 \\\\ x & \\ge -\\frac{7}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the inequality above is $x\\ge -\\frac{7}{5}.$",
